  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>The plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;be parallel to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and the intercept of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi></math>-axis is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>,</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0123_34c087fb73f2.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 194px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Now normal of the plane will be perpendicular to the given line, so by perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Y</mi></math> intercept of plane put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;in equation of plane</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Hence, equation of plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now distance of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math>.</p>"
  }
